Alleniom Utilities	
Feeder Hosting Capacity Map Export	
Publication	Alleniom Utilities Feeder Hosting Capacity Map
Published	05/15/2024
Publishing organization	Alleniom Utilities — Distribution Planning
Author	June Halloway, Distribution Planning Engineer
Contact	june.halloway@alleniom.com
Office	DER Program Office · 4200 Veldmere Boulevard, Halston, Alleron 01HA
Refresh commitment	Quarterly refresh commitment. The map is republished on a quarterly cadence with updated published available capacity values incorporating incremental planning studies and material queue additions since the prior release.
Refresh prioritization criteria	Refresh prioritization criteria: application date, capacity requested, DER category (net metering vs pure generation). Feeders with the earliest pending pre-application or application date receive priority for re-study, followed by feeders where the requested capacity is largest relative to the currently published available figure, followed by DER category weighting per the net metering vs pure generation distinction (pure-generation queue entries are weighted more heavily against feeder headroom than net-metering behind-the-meter entries at equivalent nameplate).
Basis	Feeder-level planning study using recorded peak and minimum load, existing interconnected DER of record at the time of the underlying study, and standard thermal / voltage / protection screens per Alleniom Distribution Planning methodology.
DER Category legend	"Net metering" — behind-the-meter DER netted against customer load at the point of common coupling. "Pure generation" — export-only front-of-the-meter DER. "Mixed" — feeder hosts a combination of net-metering and pure-generation interconnections.
Voltage class note	Nominal voltages given as feeder primary line-to-line kV.
Scope	Alleniom distribution system, all substations serving in-scope DER territory. Sub-transmission and transmission-connected resources excluded.
Applicability	Values are the published available capacity figures as of the publication date shown above. Applicants and pre-application requesters should consult Distribution Planning for confirmation before finalizing project sizing decisions on any feeder shown. Published values do not reflect interconnection queue activity recorded after the publication date; the active-queue register maintained by the DER Program Office is the record of that activity. A pre-application capacity response is prepared against the published value as adjusted for queue entries added since publication.
